## 10. Scanner Output Fields

When reporting a potential Security Misconfiguration, provide:

- vulnerability: Security Misconfiguration
- vulnerability_type: Debug Mode / Error Disclosure / Insecure Defaults / Missing Security Headers / Cookie Configuration / Unknown
- file: Source file containing the finding
- location: Relevant line number or configuration location
- evidence: Relevant configuration or code fragment
- configuration_source: Environment variable, configuration file, application code, or deployment setting
- affected_component: Application, framework, server, or infrastructure
- environment: Development / Testing / Production / Unknown
- explanation: Why the configuration may introduce a security weakness
- severity: Estimated severity
- confidence: Confidence in the finding
- false_positive_reason: Possible reasons the configuration is safe
- remediation: Recommended correction
- cwe: Relevant CWE identifier

